WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.820
Hi, my name is Denisse Chavez, and I’m the
chef of El Atoradero.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.480
The enchilada is a very traditional dish from
Puebla.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.940
Nobody goes to Puebla without eating enchiladas
or mole poblano.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.560
You can get enchiladas everywhere in Puebla,
and every day.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.570
But the mole poblano, with chicken or with
pork, is just for special occasions, like

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.440
birthdays or when people get married.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.739
Every restaurant says they serve "original”
Mexican food, but when you go there, it's

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.079
not original food.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.640
So over here I try to push myself to not forget
my culture.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.180
Over here we use special tortillas.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.039
I get the blue corn from Mexico.

00:00:56.039 --> 00:01:02.500
We cook the corn, and then we put it in the
molino and make fresh tortillas and fresh

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.630
masa.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:11.820
We use four tortillas to roll the chicken,
but you have to put it inside the mole to

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:12.820
get it wet.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.820
That's why we call them "enchiladas."

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.720
They have to be very wet.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.580
You can use anything you want for decoration
or the garnish.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:25.080
But the original, traditional way is avocado,
cheese, and cream—and that's it.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:30.650
The mole poblano is very traditional, but
it's also difficult to do.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.579
This recipe is from my grandma.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:34.840
I use more than six chiles.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.920
One of the chiles—we call it ancho—is
more red.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.340
Mulato is black.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.670
And then pasilla is sweet.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:48.700
If you want it more spicy, you can use chile
morita, chipotle, or pulla.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:56.080
I'm using raisins, cinnamon, garlic, cloves,
black pepper, anise, and plantains.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.980
All of those ingredients give you a nice flavor
with the chiles.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.600
It's very hard to make the mole, but it's
very good.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.480
I’m trying to do everything 100% traditional.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.020
When I go to Mexico, I’m always behind my
sister or

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:17.820
my mom.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:25.000
They cook everything from scratch. They still do the nixtamal, the fresh tortillas.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.300
So there are many, many, dishes that I can still bring.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:39.540
I love to bring original plates from my culture, and show the real Mexican food.

